 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20SP%20%20MATHEMATICS%20GR%207-9.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Factorise algebraic expressions that involve: common factors, difference of two squares, trinomials of the form x² + bx + c and ax² + bx + c where a is a common factor.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 9 factorisation worksheets: common factors, difference of two squares and factorising trinomials. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "a² − b² = (a + b)(a − b).",
 "key_sub": "Take out the HCF first.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Always take out the highest common factor first: 6x² + 9x = 3x(2x + 3).</li><li>Difference of two squares: a² − b² = (a + b)(a − b).</li><li>Trinomial x² + bx + c: find two numbers that multiply to c and add to b.</li><li>Check by expanding.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>x² − x − 12</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>−4 × 3 = −12</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>−4 + 3 = −1</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: (x − 4)(x + 3)</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part of the factor</td><td>Take out the highest common factor.</td></tr><tr><td>a² − b² = (a − b)²</td><td>It is (a + b)(a − b).</td></tr><tr><td>Signs</td><td>Check by expanding.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 9 say about factorisation?",
   "a": "Factorise algebraic expressions that involve common factors, the difference of two squares and trinomials of the form x² + bx + c and ax² + bx + c where a is a common factor."
